{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"SCOPE CORRECTION #2 (orchestrator): the hosted-openai-chat deprecation removal also requires the\nresolution cluster — src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py (_resolve_target) and\nsrc/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py (_pai_model), which currently honor/preserve hosted openai-chat.\nAdded both to file_impact. NUANCE (per _deprecations.py:105-112 and the code comments): ONLY the\nHOSTED-OpenAI openai-chat prefix/provider (no custom base_url) is the scheduled deprecation ->\nreplacement openai-responses. An EXPLICIT openai-chat with a CUSTOM base_url/endpoint (a custom\nOpenAI-compatible server whose /v1/responses support is unknown) is a SUPPORTED selection and must\nbe PRESERVED. The oracle must encode this hosted-vs-custom distinction. No other Wave-1 agent\ntouches llm/*."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788469095405204402,"uuid":"8def02cb-aa3e-4116-8015-bc3fc5d1a62a"}